@div segment A

A.1. u₅{mušen} ŋiš-gi kug-ta nam-ta#-[e₃]
#lem: u[wild goose]; ŋešgi[thicket]; kug[pure]; e[leave]
#tr.en: The pelican (?) came forth from the holy reedbeds. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 31; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 49

A.2. ŋiš-gi kug-ga-ta nam-ta#-[e₃]
#lem: ŋešgi[thicket]; kug[pure]; e[leave]
#tr.en: It came forth from the holy reedbeds. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. u₅{mušen} kug-zu ud an-šag₄-ge mu-un-zal
#lem: u[wild goose]; kugzu[wise]; ud[sun]; anšag[the interior of heaven]; zal[pass time]
#tr.en: The wise pelican (?) spent the day high in the skies. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

