A.23. in-nin₉-me-en mušen-ŋu₁₀ zar ab-du₈-še₃ gu₂ ha-ma-ab-si-si
#lem: innin[lady]; mušen[bird]; zar[sheaf (of barley)]; du[spread]; gu[neck]; si[fill]
#tr.en: @q[Nance,]{“I am the mistress, so let my birds assemble for me where the sheaves are gathered! I am @wDN{Nanše}, so let my birds assemble for me where the sheaves are gathered! Let the birds of heaven and earth stand at my service! Let every bird without a name bring offerings! Let every bird not caught in nets ……!”} 
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

